# PRIVACY POLICY

**Last updated: August 22, 2026**

This Privacy Policy explains how **MoneyNest** (“we”, “our”, or the “App”) handles information when you use our mobile application.

By using MoneyNest, you agree to the practices described in this Privacy Policy.

## 1. About MoneyNest

MoneyNest is a personal finance management application designed to help users:

* Record income and expenses.
* Organize transactions by categories and tags.
* Track recurring income and expenses.
* View spending reports and financial summaries.
* Set reminders for recurring payments or expense tracking.
* Use voice input to quickly record expenses.
* Discover meal suggestions and cooking-related content.
* Manage personal preferences such as language and currency.

MoneyNest is intended for personal financial organization and does not provide banking, investment, tax, accounting, or professional financial advice.

## 2. Information We May Process

Depending on the features you use, MoneyNest may process the following information.

### Financial Information

You may enter information such as:

* Expense amounts.
* Income amounts.
* Transaction descriptions.
* Expense and income categories.
* Tags.
* Recurring payments.
* Recurring income.
* Notes related to transactions.

This information is used only to provide the personal finance management features of MoneyNest.

MoneyNest does not request or store your:

* Bank account password.
* Credit card PIN.
* Online banking password.
* Banking authentication codes.

### Voice Input

If you choose to use voice input, MoneyNest may request access to your device microphone.

Microphone access is used only when you actively use the voice input feature.

MoneyNest does not continuously record audio in the background.

Depending on the implementation of the voice recognition service, voice data may be processed by the operating system or a third-party speech recognition provider.

### Notification Information

If you enable reminders, MoneyNest may send notifications for features such as:

* Daily expense reminders.
* Recurring expense reminders.
* Upcoming payment reminders.
* Other finance-related reminders configured by you.

You can disable notifications at any time through your device settings.

### Device and Technical Information

For application operation, security, diagnostics, or crash analysis, limited technical information may be processed, such as:

* Device type.
* Operating system version.
* App version.
* Language.
* Region.
* Crash information.
* Diagnostic information.

We do not use this information to identify you personally unless required for security, support, or legal purposes.

## 3. How We Use Information

Information processed by MoneyNest may be used to:

* Provide expense and income tracking features.
* Generate financial summaries and reports.
* Display spending statistics.
* Manage categories, tags, and recurring transactions.
* Provide personalized application settings.
* Process voice-based expense entry.
* Send reminders requested by the user.
* Improve application stability and performance.
* Diagnose technical issues.
* Prevent misuse or security issues.

We do not sell your personal information.

## 4. Personal Financial Data

The financial information entered into MoneyNest is provided directly by you.

This information is used to help you organize and understand your personal finances.

MoneyNest is not a financial institution and does not have access to your bank accounts unless a future feature explicitly requires such access and you provide separate permission.

Any financial reports, statistics, projections, or recommendations generated by MoneyNest are for informational purposes only.

You remain responsible for your own financial decisions.

## 5. Meal Suggestions and Cooking Content

MoneyNest may provide meal recommendations, recipes, ingredients, estimated prices, or cooking-related information.

This information is provided for general informational purposes.

Ingredient prices, cooking times, nutritional information, or estimated costs may vary depending on:

* Location.
* Store.
* Season.
* Market conditions.
* Product brand.
* Portion size.

MoneyNest does not guarantee that estimated prices or cooking information will always be completely accurate.

Users should independently verify information when necessary.

## 6. Data Storage

Depending on the version and features of MoneyNest, data may be stored:

* Locally on your device.
* On servers operated by us or our service providers.
* Through services provided by the mobile operating system.

We take reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect information against unauthorized access, loss, misuse, alteration, or disclosure.

However, no method of electronic storage or transmission is completely secure.

## 7. Third-Party Services

MoneyNest may use third-party services to provide features such as:

* Crash reporting.
* Analytics.
* Push notifications.
* Speech recognition.
* Cloud infrastructure.
* Application performance monitoring.

These third-party services may process limited information according to their own privacy policies.

Examples may include services provided by:

* Apple.
* Google.
* Firebase.
* Cloud infrastructure providers.

The specific services used may change as MoneyNest develops.

We encourage users to review the privacy policies of relevant third-party services.

## 8. Permissions

MoneyNest may request certain device permissions only when required for specific features.

### Microphone

Used for voice-based expense entry.

### Notifications

Used to send expense reminders, recurring payment reminders, and other notifications selected by the user.

MoneyNest will not access these permissions without authorization from the device operating system.

You can revoke permissions at any time through your device settings.

## 9. Data Sharing

We do not sell, rent, or trade users' personal information.

Information may only be shared when necessary:

* With service providers required to operate MoneyNest.
* To protect the security of the App.
* To investigate fraud or abuse.
* To comply with applicable laws or legal requests.
* To protect our legal rights or the safety of users.

Service providers are expected to process information only as necessary to provide their services.

## 10. Data Retention

We retain information only for as long as necessary to provide MoneyNest's features, comply with legal obligations, resolve disputes, or protect the security of the service.

If information is stored only on your device, deleting MoneyNest may remove that locally stored information.

If MoneyNest uses server-side storage, users may request deletion of applicable personal data by contacting us.

## 11. Data Deletion

You may delete individual financial records directly within MoneyNest where deletion functionality is available.

If you would like to request deletion of personal information stored on our servers, please contact:

**Email:** [2t.global921@gmail.com](mailto:2t.global921@gmail.com)

We may need to verify the request before processing it.

## 12. Children's Privacy

MoneyNest is not specifically designed for children under the minimum age required by applicable law.

We do not knowingly collect personal information from children without appropriate authorization.

If you believe that a child has provided personal information to us, please contact us so that we can review and remove the information where required.

## 13. Security

We use reasonable safeguards designed to protect information processed by MoneyNest.

However, users are also responsible for:

* Protecting access to their device.
* Using device security features such as passcodes, Face ID, Touch ID, or equivalent protections.
* Avoiding sharing sensitive information with unauthorized individuals.

## 14. International Users

MoneyNest may be available in multiple countries and languages.

Information may be processed in countries other than your country of residence depending on the infrastructure or service providers used by the App.

Where required, we take reasonable measures to protect information in accordance with applicable privacy requirements.

## 15. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy when:

* New features are introduced.
* Data processing practices change.
* Legal or regulatory requirements change.
* Third-party services change.

The updated version will be published with a revised “Last updated” date.

We encourage users to periodically review this Privacy Policy.

## 16. Contact Us

If you have questions, privacy concerns, or data deletion requests, please contact:

**App:** MoneyNest
**Email:** [2t.global921@gmail.com](mailto:2t.global921@gmail.com)

